"Cinematic photorealistic fantasy, where lost things go: every hairpin, bobby pin and hair tie that ever vanished from a wrist, a pocket or a bathroom sink ends up in this one ancient tree. A huge old oak tree standing alone in a misty meadow at sunrise, its branches wrapped and decorated with thousands of real lost hair accessories: colorful scrunchies, black elastic hair ties, glittering hairpins, butterfly clips, pearl barrettes, bobby pins shining like dew. A family of real black-and-white magpies, the famous collectors of shiny things, are the keepers of the tree: one magpie carries a bright pink scrunchie in its beak back to the tree, another carefully sorts a row of shiny hairpins on a branch, a young magpie wears a small hair tie around its neck like a necklace. Camera: medium-wide eye-level shot, 50mm lens, deep focus, the tree filling the frame, the magpie with the pink scrunchie flying in the foreground left. Lighting: soft golden sunrise light glowing through the mist, sparkling highlights on the metal pins and glitter clips. Color palette: misty green, golden sunrise, black-and-white magpies, pastel scrunchie colors, silver pins, fine film grain. " + LOOK,
